1. Nf3 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. g3 Bg7 4. Bg2 d6 5. O-O O-O 6. Nc3 e5 7. d3 a5 8. b3 Nc6 9. Bb2 Re8 10. Rc1 Bd7 11. h3 Nh5 12. e3 Ne7 13. d4 Nc6 14. dxe5 dxe5 15. Ne4 Qc8 16. g4 Nf6 17. Nc5 Rd8 18. Nxd7 Rxd7 19. Qc2 Nb4 20. Qb1 Nd3 21. Rcd1 Nxb2 22. Qxb2 e4 23. Nd4 c5 24. Nb5 Nxg4 25. Qc2 Ne5 26. Qxe4 f5 27. Qh4 Kh8 28. f4 Nd3 29. Bd5 Nb4 30. Be6 Qd8 31. Qxd8+ Rdxd8 32. Nd6 Rdb8 33. Nf7+ {... at this point the electronic board goes haywire and records an illegal move followed by a lot of other moves as text: h6 Rd7+ Kh7 a4 Nc2 Kf2 Re8 Rd6 Ra6 Rxa6 bxa6 Bd5 Nxe3 Re1 Bd4 Kf3 Rb8 Rxe3 Bxe3 Kxe3 Rxb3+ Kf2 Rxh3 Ne5 Ra3 Bc6 g5 fxg5 hxg5 Nd7 g4 Nxc5 f4 Ne6 Ra2+ Kf1 f3 c5 g3 Bxf3 Rf2+ Kg1 Kg6 Be4+ Kf6 Nc7 Ra2 Bc6 Rc2 Nxa6 Ke5 Bb7 Kd4 c6 Rb2 c7... but perhaps, with a nudge in the right direction, we can make sense of them, thus:} Kg8 34. Ng5+ Kh8 35. Rd7 {and now we can follow the moves recorded in the text (well, more or less)...} h6 36. Nf7+ Kh7 37. a4 Nc2 38. Kf2 Re8 39. Rd6 Ra6 40. Rxa6 bxa6 41. Bd5 Nxe3 42. Re1 Bd4 43. Kf3 Rb8 44. Rxe3 Bxe3 45. Kxe3 Rxb3+ 46. Kf2 Rxh3 47. Ne5 Ra3 48. Bc6 g5 49. fxg5 hxg5 50. Nd7 g4 51. Nxc5 f4 52. Ne6 Ra2+ 53. Kf1 f3 54. c5 g3 $4 55. Bxf3 Rf2+ {One suspects that Black now noticed his planned ...Rxf3 fails to Ng5+} 56. Kg1 Kg6 57. Be4+ Kf6 58. Nc7 Ra2 59. Bc6 Rc2 60. Nxa6 Ke5 61. Bb7 Kd4 62. c6 Rb2 63. c7 {... I wonder if that is what happened?! JS} 1-0

